  "rendered": {
    "title": "Pay-per-call LLM access and a new Claude Fable tier",
    "intro": "Today's nightly opens up Aura's LLM router to x402-based micropayments, tightens the billing client against unsafe service endpoints, and brings Anthropic's Claude Fable 5 into the managed model lineup.",
    "entries": [
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-1",
        "time_label": "9:25 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-09T04:25:43.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-09T04:25:43.000Z",
        "title": "x402 micropayment endpoint for public LLM access",
        "summary": "Aura's server now exposes a paid, x402-protected public chat completions API that settles against z-billing usage quotes.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added a new `/api/public/x402/v1/chat/completions` endpoint and matching `/v1/models` listing, implementing the x402 protocol directly in the Axum router so anonymous callers can pay per request without an account.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Defaults to the `upto` scheme with a $0.02 ceiling against Base Sepolia USDC, settling the real z-billing usage quote per call; operators can override price, scheme, network, asset, facilitator, and timeouts via the new `AURA_X402_*` environment variables documented in the README.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Introduced guardrails on the public surface including a configurable model allowlist, a default `aura-claude-haiku-4-5` model, max-token caps, message size and count limits, and a 120s completion timeout.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended the billing client with a usage-quote path (`LlmUsageQuote`) so the x402 handler can convert LLM token usage into a settled dollar amount.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "c0684ba57ba0d4472dde63fab41f0d8e1c13c909"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-3",
        "time_label": "8:40 AM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-09T15:40:50.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-09T15:40:50.000Z",
        "title": "Billing client now refuses insecure service URLs",
        "summary": "The billing HTTP client validates its configured base URL before issuing any request, closing off accidental plaintext or private-network calls.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Requests now go through a new `service_url` builder that parses the base URL with `url::Url`, normalizes trailing slashes, and rejects anything that isn't HTTPS to a public host — `http://`, loopback, RFC1918, link-local, and embedded `user:pass@` credentials all return the new `InsecureServiceUrl` error.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "46c9194757af4ce7cc4d823487bdc5278df6d3f6"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Debug and test builds retain an explicit carve-out for `http://localhost` and `127.0.0.1` so local development against a mock billing service still works.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "46c9194757af4ce7cc4d823487bdc5278df6d3f6"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "batch_id": "entry-4",
        "time_label": "3:36 PM",
        "started_at": "2026-06-09T22:36:31.000Z",
        "ended_at": "2026-06-09T22:36:31.000Z",
        "title": "Claude Fable 5 joins the managed Anthropic lineup",
        "summary": "Anthropic's new Fable-class model is wired into Aura's interface with pricing, normalization, and model-picker metadata.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added `aura-claude-fable-5` as a featured Opus-tier Anthropic chat model with a 1M-token context window, 10× credit multiplier, and a Mythos-class description in the model picker.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5352382459a8f8fc6748752cca8149f1b1967b91"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Registered Claude Fable 5 pricing at $10 input / $50 output per million tokens (with $12.50 cache-write and $1 cache-read) in both the runtime pricing table and the benchmark pricing script.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5352382459a8f8fc6748752cca8149f1b1967b91"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Taught the model-id normalizer to map raw `claude-fable-5` and legacy ids onto the Aura-managed `aura-claude-fable-5`, so persisted selections and benchmark lookups resolve consistently.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "5352382459a8f8fc6748752cca8149f1b1967b91"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          }
        ]
      }
